The following items in examples/max-m10s-breakout-revc/ are copied from, or
derived from, the KiCad official symbol and footprint libraries (KiCad 10.0.6).
They remain under CC-BY-SA 4.0 with the KiCad libraries exception. The exception
means designs that use these parts (schematics, boards, fabrication outputs) are
not bound by CC-BY-SA; the library files themselves are.

symbols/PassiveGNSS.kicad_sym
  Identical to the official symbol:
    R, C, D, LED                 <- Device:R, Device:C, Device:D, Device:LED
    TestPoint                    <- Connector:TestPoint
    PWR_FLAG                     <- power:PWR_FLAG
  Same graphics, footprint filters changed:
    C_Polarized, D_TVS           <- Device:C_Polarized, Device:D_TVS
    Conn_01x06                   <- Connector_Generic:Conn_01x06
    Conn_Coaxial                 <- Connector:Conn_Coaxial

footprints/PassiveGNSS.pretty/
  Renamed, 3D model reference removed, pads unchanged:
    C_0603                       <- Capacitor_SMD:C_0603_1608Metric
    R_0603                       <- Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric
    LED_0603                     <- LED_SMD:LED_0603_1608Metric
    SOT23                        <- Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23
  Renamed, otherwise identical:
    Fiducial_1mm                 <- Fiducial:Fiducial_1mm_Mask3mm
    ToolingHole_2mm              <- MountingHole:MountingHole_2mm
    TestPoint                    <- TestPoint:TestPoint_Pad_D1.0mm
  Renamed, silkscreen lines moved to F.Fab:
    Header_1x06                  <- Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_1x06_P2.54mm_Vertical

Made for this project (MIT): symbols MAX_M10S, BAS116, Q_NMOS_GSD; footprints
MAX_M10S, PESD3V3C1BSF, ADCM_S05R5SA, CPH3225A, MHF_I. The vendor-specific
footprints were drawn from the manufacturers' published land patterns, which
are not included here.

